[center][size=5][color=#E0B062][b]Magic Quest Log[/b][/color][/size]
[size=3][i]Quest and deed atlas for Middle-earth – right inside the game[/i][/size]

[b]15,209 quests[/b]  •  [b]5,534 deeds[/b]  •  [b]English · Deutsch · Français[/b]
Companion website: [url=https://llb.sirhexalot.de][b]LOTRO Log Book[/b][/url][/center]

[size=4][color=#E0B062][b]What is this?[/b][/color][/size]
Magic Quest Log shows you every quest and deed in Middle-earth, sorted by where it happens, with the full text and its steps – and it remembers what you have already done.
No browser tab, no second monitor, no outside program: [b]one window in the game[/b].

[size=4][color=#E0B062][b]What it does[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Everything in one tree.[/b] Two levels only: region (or epic volume), then area. An area lists its quests under foldable sections – the area itself, sub-areas, quest groups.
[*][b]Search[/b] for any part of a name or an area. Small spelling differences don't matter: "ker izel" finds "Kêr Izel".
[*][b]No spoilers.[/b] You see level, quest giver, requirements, quest chain and description. Steps and objectives only when you ask for them – for that one quest.
[*][b]Filter[/b] with four buttons: All, Open, Done, Available. "Available" checks your level and earlier quests.
[*][b]See your progress.[/b] Anything you finish is counted right away. Every branch shows "done / total", deed counters show "44/75", finished entries get a [color=#7FBF6A]green check[/color].
[*][b]Show it on the map.[/b] One click opens MoorMap where the quest giver stands, or at the first objective when you show them – only where the position is known. No guessed pins.
[*][b]Facts from the game.[/b] LOTRO points of deeds, daily, repeatable, fellowship, instance, time limit.
[*][b]Several characters.[/b] A switch appears as soon as you have more than one.
[/list]
[i]Not included: items, recipes, equipment, an own map.[/i]

[size=4][color=#E0B062][b]Installing[/b][/color][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Unzip the download into the game's [b]Plugins[/b] folder (where [i]Compendium[/i] or [i]GaranStuff[/i] live). Afterwards [font=Courier New]Plugins\MagicQuestLog\MagicQuestLog.plugin[/font] must exist.
[*]Start the game.
[*]Load the plugin: [font=Courier New]/plugins load MagicQuestLog[/font]
German client: [font=Courier New]/zusatzmodule laden MagicQuestLog[/font] – or simply restart the game.
[*]Type [font=Courier New][b]/mql[/b][/font] to open the window.
[/list]
Only the map button needs [url=https://www.lotrointerface.com/downloads/info532-MoorMap.html]MoorMap[/url] by Garan; everything else works without it.

[size=4][color=#E0B062][b]Your older quests and deeds[/b][/color][/size]
The plugin counts what you finish [b]from the moment it is installed[/b]. Older progress comes from [b]LOTRO Companion[/b] through the free [url=https://llb.sirhexalot.de][b]LOTRO Log Book[/b][/url] website. Skip this if you don't care about old entries.
[list=1]
[*]In [url=https://sourceforge.net/projects/lotrocompanion/]LOTRO Companion[/url]: log in your character, then [b]Misc → Import from LOTRO…[/b], [i]Refresh[/i], [i]Start[/i].
[*]Open [url=https://llb.sirhexalot.de/spielstand.html]llb.sirhexalot.de/spielstand.html[/url] and choose Companion's [b]characters[/b] folder. It is read [b]only in your browser[/b] – nothing is uploaded.
[*]Click [b]Write into the LOTRO folder[/b] (Chrome, Edge) or [b]Download as zip[/b] and unpack it into the game's [b]PluginData[/b] folder.
[*]Open the Magic Quest Log window. Done – no restart needed.
[/list]
[color=#9FB7CF]Bonus on the website: a map of quests and deeds, deed counters ("44/75"), your reputation with every faction and your crafting tiers – per character.[/color]

[b]Collecting deeds above all?[/b] Have a look at [url=https://www.lotrointerface.com/downloads/info1139-DeedTracker.html]Deed Tracker[/url] by b414213562 – a mature plugin just for deeds. Both work side by side.

[size=4][color=#E0B062][b]Good to know[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Window and start icon remember their place; the icon opens or hides the window.
[*]Plugin not listed? [font=Courier New]/plugins refresh[/font] (German: [font=Courier New]/zusatzmodule aktualisieren[/font]), then load it.
[*]The catalogs are large (about 100 MB, three languages) – the first load takes a moment.
[/list]

[size=4][color=#E0B062][b]Changes[/b][/color][/size]
[b]0.3.0[/b] – what the LOTRO Log Book shows, now in the plugin
[list]
[*]No spoilers: objectives per quest on request; MoorMap points at the quest giver.
[*]Quest giver, requirements, quest chain, LOTRO points, daily/repeatable, "available" filter.
[*]Tree with two levels and foldable sections; four filter buttons.
[*]More positions: 12,010 quests with an objective, 6,621 with the giver's place.
[/list]
[b]0.2.0[/b] – progress from LOTRO Companion, several characters
[list]
[*]Older progress comes from LOTRO Companion through the website, converted in your browser. The separate tool from 0.1.x is gone.
[*]Character switch in the window; a new import is picked up whenever you open it.
[*]Live progress is kept per character; progress from 0.1.x is taken over.
[/list]
[b]0.1.2[/b] – counters show what is still possible: session plays and ruled-out alternatives are marked and no longer counted.
[b]0.1.1[/b] – long names wrap onto a second line; territories no longer appear twice.
[b]0.1.0[/b] – first release.
